Save Format as Per-Turn Snapshots

Date: 2025-08-17

Status: Accepted

Context: We need reliable saves/loads for fast iteration; event-log replays add complexity early.

Decision: Use per-turn snapshots (JSON or msgpack) containing header (ids, schema, seed), state (world/entities/story flags/visibility), and meta (timings, counts). Keep a rolling window (e.g., last 20) plus manual milestones. Include a content hash for integrity.

Consequences:

Simple, debuggable saves; quick rollback.

Larger files than event logs; diffs less compact.

Alternatives considered: Event-sourced log (compact/replayable; higher engineering cost), hybrid (snapshots + periodic deltas).

Notes/Follow-ups: Add JSON Schemas; consider compression; introduce Alembic when ORM stabilizes.
